{"_id":"6a2feeb32204ffbc59e5a2a2","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"olniprgaL7l-9YhwbFfmN","description":"# Tuples\n\nTuples are ordered, immutable sequences. Unlike lists, their contents cannot be changed after creation. They are used to represent fixed collections of values, such as coordinate pairs, function return values, and dictionary keys where immutability is required.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Tuple","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/datastructures.html#tuples-and-sequences","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb6f"},{"type":"video","title":"Python Tuples","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w6hL_dszMxk","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb70"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:23:15.410Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/olniprgaL7l-9YhwbFfmN.md"}